Interesting: my monk was one of the few characters that ascended first
try.

Starting with speed is quite nice.  I didn't run the protection
racket, but I did buy protection as quickly as I could.  Credit
cloning helps.  Martial Arts at Grand Master seemed to do a fair
amount of damage.  My spellbook was protection.  perhaps it would have
been my 3rd choice out of sleep, healing, and protection, but
regardless of which one you get, don't forget to use it.  I found it
so much easier to fight elf-lords at AC -7 than AC 0.

My biggest concern in the middle game was a lack of MR.  I think I got
a throne wish or magic lamp wish at some point for the EoA.  Once I
got to XL 14 or so, I reverse genocided some silver dragons and played
my monk like I play any other character:  SDSM, MR artifact, and +7
artifact weapon.  At that point, the game becomes easy again.  The
hard part is getting from XL 9 (which you can easily get above DL 7
without risking polymorphing through your robe) to getting enough
stuff where you can safely reverse genocide silver dragons and get
yourself a +7 artifact weapon that you can hit with while wearing your
newly enchanted SDSM.  Don't forget to get 18 Dexterity and 18/
something strength to help with landing hits.

Before I got the EoA, I think I mostly wore a dwarvish cloak around.
When hard monsters showed up, I'd retreat to the previous level, put
on my robe, cast protection, put the cloak back on, and then go
fight.

Incidentally, don't worry about what you eat; the penalty for eating
meat is trivial.



